title: "Button popularity alone explains the dogs' non-random networks"
abstract: "A pre-registered re-test of the 2024 finding that soundboard-trained dogs combine buttons in non-random networks found that unequal button use, with no preference for any pairing, produces an even more non-random-looking index than the dogs' own networks. Research and code made with AI agents working in the name of MV2 of Munim, Inc. Code licensed Apache-2.0; text and data CC BY 4.0 unless a file says otherwise."
